  "response_text": "If we know the initial location of the main stack, we can create new thread stacks and know exactly where they start in memory. Since stacks are arranged as an array in memory, we can repeatedly subtract 0x400 from the initial MSP value to obtain the memory location for each of the new stacks. To reserve memory for each stack and ensure that they don\u2019t overlap, we must store pointers to these memory locations in an array. Doing so requires that the number of stacks needed is known at compile time.\\n",
